-- Ordered quest guidance; source 967020b2b8ca645afcaf90d9bbe5a1b64673947d; generated 2026-10-20.
QuestGuidance.Register("en",31,{
[961]="700515FD\n1\tCollect spiderlings at Scary (total: 12)\tGreenfield spiderlings can be found in Scary and its quarry. Hoping to make some of the cotton-webbed bushes at Wistmead more convincing, Iris Tunnelly has asked you to collect spiderlings at Scary.\n2\tTalk to Iris Tunnelly\tIris Tunnelly can be found in Wistmead. You have gathered a number of spiderlings in Scary and you should now return to Iris Tunnelly.\n3\tDeliver spiderlings into curiously empty webs in Wistmead (total: 4)\tCuriously empty webbing can be found on bushes throughout Wistmead. Iris Tunnelly has asked you to put the spiderlings you found into a few of the webbed bushes in Wistmead.\n4\tTalk to Iris Tunnelly\tIris Tunnelly can be found in Wistmead. You have filled several webbed bushes with spiders. You should now return to Iris Tunnelly.\n",
[962]="70043056\n1\tTalk to Merenir\tMerenir stands by the entrance to Imloth Melui. Lady Vanyalos has asked you to talk to Merenir, who has one last favour to ask you before you depart Imloth Melui.\n2\tFind Dindal at the look-out\tDindal the scout can be found high up in a secluded look-out, which can be reached by turning north off the east road from Imloth Melui. Merenir has asked you to visit his scout, Dindal, at the look-out and assist in any way that you can.\n3\tGaze north-east from the look-out\tDindal the scout can be found high up in a secluded look-out, which can be reached by turning north off the east road from Imloth Melui. Dindal has asked you to stand by his side and look out to the north-east.\n4\tTalk to Dindal\tDindal the scout can be found high up in a secluded look-out, which can be reached by turning north off the east road from Imloth Melui. Now that you have looked out to the north-east, you should talk to Dindal again.\n",
[963]="700142F9\n1\tFind the goblin-tribe\tThe goblin-camp can be found through a crack in the wall above the eastern stair. Túbi Thickfist has asked you to locate the goblin-camp.\n2\tSpeak with the dwarf near the goblin camp of Snaga-maudhûl\tJarmárr is near the goblin camp of Snaga-maudhûl. You have located the goblin-tribe and heard the voice the chieftain spoke of. You should speak with the dwarf near the road.\n",
[964]="70055179\n1\tTalk to Faramir\tFaramir can be found outside Uialrond, the Dome of Evening. Faramir is prepared to enter Uialrond and confront whatever evils lurk within. You should talk to Faramir when you are ready.\n2\tTalk to Faramir\030Talk to Éowyn\tFaramir and Éowyn can be found outside Uialrond, the Dome of Evening in the Circle of Death. You have discovered a beacon of hope within Minas Morgul and heartened the Rangers of Ithilien. You should talk to Faramir and Éowyn.\n",
[965]="7006566E\n1\tTalk to Captain Thandor\tCelebros has asked you to bring some sealed orders and a lockbox to Captain Thandor. He stands watch near the East Pelargir gates.\n2\tTalk to Nasar\tYou still have papers to deliver to Nasar and his companions. You should return to them near the West Pelargir gates.\n",
[966]="7005A5F8\n1\tTalk to Mekhnet\tA recently-arrived Mekhnet wishes to speak with you.\n2\tDefeat Orc-sentries (total: 7)\tOrc-sentries can be found in Târ-kútoz. You should defeat them to ensure easier access to Atrad-zarakh later.\n3\tTalk to Lúka\tYou have defeated as many Orc-sentries as you could find. You should report back to Lúka in Ashmargathâl.\n",
[967]="7002BFE1\n1\tDefeat Hafoc\tThe brigand captain can be found somewhere within Helstor, north of Etheburg in the Brown Lands. Céola has asked you to confront the leader of the brigands in the Brown Lands.\n2\tTalk to Céola at Etheburg in the Brown Lands\tCéola is at Etheburg in the Brown Lands, south of Helstor. You should return to Céola with news of your victory.\n",
[968]="7006C6F6\n1\tMeet Raphûz at Igbâl's home in Jirush\tRaphûz wants you to meet him at Igbâl's home in Jirush when he presents the merchant with the treasure he acquired from Nirgambâr.\n2\tSpeak with Galamê in Igbâl's home in Jirush\tRaphûz is engaged in discussion with Igbâl. Galamê motioned to you. You should speak with Galamê at Igbâl's home in Jirush.\n3\tSpeak with Raphûz in Igbâl's home in Jirush\tGalamê informed you that Ashâmi went missing soon after you and Raphûz departed for Nirgambâr. He suggested you speak with your friend Raphûz at Igbâl's home to see what he learned and to help him.\n4\tSpeak with Galamê at Igbâl's home in Jirush\tGalamê overheard Raphûz's comment and motioned you to attend him.\n5\tSpeak with Raphûz at Igbâl's home in Jirush\tGalamê's warning was clear. If Raphûz makes a scene here, he will create enemies where he does not want them. Speak to the young man in Igbâl's home.\n6\tSpeak with Raphûz at his home in Jirush\tRaphûz wisely chose to continue his conversation out of earshot of Igbâl, Ardub, and Tâlsari. He waits your arrival at his home in Jirush.\n",
[969]="7001792B\n1\tBring the collected items to Hrotha at Ost Guruth in the Lone-lands\030Collect invader's breastplates (total: 12)\030Collect Bryok's spear\tAngmarim can be found at Annúminas in Evendim. Bryok dwells in Forochel. Hrotha wishes you to bring the breastplates from the Angmarim invaders in Annúminas and the spear of Bryok the Gauradan.\n2\tBring the collected items to Hrotha at Ost Guruth in the Lone-lands\030Collect revered wight-remains (total: 10)\030Collect gem-encrusted nails (total: 20)\tWights can be found in Angmar, Forochel, Annúminas, and Helegrod. Cave-claws can be found in Angmar and Sarnúr in Ered Luin. Hrotha requires the remains of wights and the talons of a like number of Gorothlad cave-claws.\n3\tBring the collected items to Hrotha at Ost Guruth in the Lone-lands\030Collect a bloodstained tally stick\030Collect a crimson Gorthorog-horn\tGríshakrum, Kughûrz, and Dafrim may be found at Urugarth. Barashal dwells in Carn Dûm. Hrotha needs a tally-stick from the Orcs of the Ongbúrz and the horn of Barashal the Gorthorog.\n",
[970]="70021ADF\n1\tTalk to Aedh at the Lhanuch crafting hall\tAedh may be found in the crafting hall. You should speak with Aedh to learn if there is any way to reforge Penlhun's axe.\n2\tBring Penlhun's axe to the mad dwarf in Thrór's Coomb\030Repair Penlhun's axe\tThe mad dwarf dwells somewhere in the mountains surrounding Thrór's Coomb, far to the east of Lhanuch. Aedh told you to seek out a mad dwarf in the valley of Thrór's Coomb and see if he can repair Penlhun's axe. Alternatively, if you are a master weaponsmith, you might attempt to repair the axe yourself at the forge in Lhanuch.\n3\tBring the axe to Penlhun\tPenlhun Brehur is at the Brenin's Hall in Lhanuch, far to the west of Thrór's Coomb. You should return to Penlhun with his father's axe.\n",
[971]="700000B0\n1\tTalk to Dorset Oakes\tDorset Oakes is often deep in contemplation at the Yellow Tree, south-east of the village of Staddle in Bree-land. You have been told to speak with Dorset Oakes in the hope that the Lore-master may be able to instruct you.\n2\tUse Book-shelves\030Collect Benton's Catalogue, Page One\030Collect Benton's Catalogue, Page Two\tDorset Oakes is at the Yellow Tree, south-east of the village of Staddle. Dorset Oakes has asked for your help in locating the book \"On the Hardiness of Animals in the Wilderness,\" and has told you to speak with him when you are ready. He mentioned that the three pages of his father's catalogue would make finding the book much easier.\n3\tBring the book he sought to Dorset Oakes\tDorset Oakes is often deep in contemplation at the Yellow Tree, south-east of the village of Staddle in Breeland. Dorset is waiting to speak with you after your successful retrieval of the book he sought.\n",
[972]="70032BA9\n1\tPick up a barrel of ale\tAle can be found near Foreman Mögr in the Twenty-first Hall. You should collect some ale and bring it to the workers and guards so that they may celebrate their victory.\n2\tDwarf-builders and guards can be found around the Twenty-first Hall. You should bring ale to the builders and guards on behalf of Foreman Mögr, who believes Zelem-melek is won for the dwarves.\t\n3\tBring ale to Reinn\tReinn is in the Twenty-first Hall of Moria, not far from Mögr. You should bring ale to Reinn.\n4\tReturn to Mögr\tForeman Mögr is in the Twenty-first Hall of Moria. You should speak with Mögr.\n",
[973]="70032BAC\n1\tPatrol the west side of the hall\030Patrol the south side of the hall\030Patrol the east side of the hall\tThe Twenty-first Hall is an enormous pillared hall covering northern Zelem-melek. You should patrol the hall and see if enemies are about.\n2\tReturn to Mögr with your findings\tMögr is in the Twenty-first Hall of Moria. You should return to Mögr with a report of what you saw on your patrol.\n3\tTalk to Reinn\tReinn is in the Twenty-first Hall. You should hear what Reinn thinks of your findings.\n",
[974]="70027ABB\n1\tWarn Elder Riagán of the Dragon-clan's intent\030If you and Blodwen become separated, use the whistle to call her back\tLhan Tarren is upriver from the Herd-lands. You must escape the Herd-lands with Blodwen to warn your friends at Lhan Tarren of the peril that hurtles towards them.\n2\tSpeak with Blodwen\030If you and Blodwen become separated, use the whistle to call her back\tBlodwen is at your side in Lhan Tarren. You should speak with Blodwen.\n",
[975]="7002EF07\n1\tTalk to Máthild\t\n2\tTalk to Máthild\tMáthild is hiding near the Mead Hall of Thornhope. You escort Máthild to safety.\n3\tTalk to Máthild at Béortnoth's camp.\tMáthild is at Béortnoth's camp, outside of Thornhope. You should speak with Máthild when you return to Béortnoth's camp.\n",
[976]="700515F9\n1\tTalk to Ermentrude Haybank\030Talk to Halinard Bunce\030Talk to Iris Tunnelly\tErmentrude Haybank, Halinard Bunce, and Iris Tunnelly can be found in Wistmead. Walaric Goldworthy has asked you to explore Wistmead and acquaint yourself with the other festival-hands. You should take a look around.\n2\tTalk to Walaric Goldworthy\tWalaric Goldworthy can be found in Wistmead. You have explored Wistmead and become acquainted with the other members of his team. You should return to Walaric Goldworthy before joining in the festivities at Wistmead.\n",
[977]="7001CEF3\n1\tDefeat spiders in the Dourstocks (total: 10)\tSpiders can be found throughout the Dourstocks. You should defeat many spiders to make the Dourstocks safer for the Malledhrim who wish to travel unhindered.\n2\tTalk to Fernachar at the Haunted Inn\tFernachar can be found in the Haunted Inn in the Dourstocks. You should return to Fernachar with word of your success against the spiders.\n",
[978]="70028C6C\n1\tFind Cadthorn\tThe missing messenger might be found somewhere to the north and west of Forthbrond. Ardwyn has asked you to find Cadforn, a messenger who is late returning to Forthbrond.\n2\tDeliver Cadthorn's message to Ardwyn at Forthbrond\tArdwyn is at Forthbrond, to the south and east of Cadthorn's position. You should return to Ardwyn with Cadthorn's message.\n",
[979]="700193AE\n1\tTalk to Laenin the Glade-watcher at Celondim\tHurry back to Celondim and speak with Laenin the Glade-watcher. Your discovery of a wolf-collar hewn by goblin crafters has proven a frightening occurrence to the glade wardens. You have been charged with bringing this news to their leader in the Elf-port of Celondim.\n",
[980]="7003043F\n1\tGather wood from the abandoned worksite (total: 7)\tWood can be found in the Warg-infested worksite east of Floodwend. You should collect wood from the abandoned worksite.\n2\tBring the wood to Radwig in Floodwend\tRadwig can be found in the Mead Hall of Floodwend. You should return to Radwig with the wood you gathered from the Worksite.\n",
[981]="70027174\n1\tSearch the first patrol point\tThe first patrol point lies to the south of Barnavon at Lhun Avanc. Gwilum has asked you to patrol Carreglyn and discover whence came the Warg-riders plaguing his clan's land.\n2\tSearch the second patrol point\tThe second patrol point is at the Barnavon mine, far to the east of Barnavon-town. Gwilum has asked you to patrol Carreglyn and discover whence came the Warg-riders plaguing his clan's land.\n3\tSearch the third patrol point\tThe third patrol point is at Hen Turrau, an old watchtower upon the hill west of the Barnavon Mine. Gwilum has asked you to patrol Carreglyn and discover whence came the Warg-riders plaguing his clan's land.\n4\tSearch the fourth patrol point\tThe fourth patrol point is at Munfaeril's Shrine, upon the lake far to the north-west of Hen Turrau. Gwilum has asked you to patrol Carreglyn and discover whence came the Warg-riders plaguing his clan's land.\n5\tTalk to Gwilum at Barnavon\tGwilum is at the gate of Barnavon. You should return to Gwilum with news of your discoveries.\n",
[982]="7000C086\n1\tEnter the caves\tA fearsome worm is deep within the caves.\n2\tDefeat the fearsome worm in the caves\tA great and fearsome worm must reside deeper within these caves. Find the worm deep in the caves.\n3\tTalk to Thorgest\tThorgest's dwelling is to the north-west of the worm-caves. You should return to Thorgest and inform him that Ruinuan is dead, slain by your hands.\n",
[983]="700460AD\n1\tDisperse well-wishers (total: 10)\tTorchún has asked you to disperse visiting well-wishers inside and outside the Houses of Healing, on the Sixth Circle of Minas Tirith.\n2\tReturn to Torchún\tYou should return to Torchún outside of the Houses of Healing and let him know you have dispersed a number of visiting well-wishers.\n",
[984]="7006C57C\n1\tGo to the location Nangar described beneath the Ordâkhai encampment\tNangar directed you to meet him beneath the Ordâkhai camp on the plateau by following a hidden path at south-western edge of the plateau. You will help provide a distraction for him.\n2\tSpeak with Nangar at the foot of the hidden path\tNangar signaled you when you arrived beneath the Ordâkhai encampment. You should speak with him.\n3\tDefeat Ordâkhai dôla ([see journal]/2)\030Defeat Ordâkhai jackal-keepers ([see journal]/4)\030Defeat other Ordâkhai warriors at the encampment north of Jirush ([see journal]/14)\tNangar stole into the encampment and vanished from sight. You are to assault the Ordâkhai encampment providing him a distraction long enough to go about finding their plans.\n4\tReturn to the foot of hidden path beneath the Ordâkhai encampment\tYou fought back the Ordâkhai and, hopefully, provided Nangar enough time and distraction to acquire the plans. Return to the hidden path at the south-western foot of the plateau beneath the Ordâkhai encampment to speak with him.\n5\tTalk to Nangar\tNangar waits for you along the hidden path beneath the Ordâkhai encampment. Speak with him to learn how successful you both were in your actions.\n6\tTalk to Nangar\tAfter speaking with Nangar near the Ordâkhai encampment, he asked to speak with you more openly at this home in the relative safety of Jirush.\n",
[985]="70017922\n1\tBring the collected items to Dardúr at Gondamon\030Collect Glâd Ereg vines (total: 12)\030Collect Helchuan's hide\tHuorns and prowlers dwell in Glâd Ereg in Eregion. Helchuan prowls near the springs north of Zigilgund in Forochel. Dardúr wishes you to bring him vines gathered from the creatures of nature in Eregion and the hide of the cold-worm Helchuan.\n2\tBring the collected items to Dardúr at Gondamon\030Collect rotted barghest paws (total: 10)\030Collect corrosive droplets (total: 20)\tBarghests can be found in Angmar. Brimstone-leeches can be found in Angmar. Dardúr now requires barghest paws and drops of brimstone-leech ichor.\n3\tBring the collected items to Dardúr at Gondamon\030Collect an ashen Gorthorog-horn\030Collect a Badge of Command\tLagmâs dwells at Urugarth and Târlug may be found at Carn Dûm in Angmar. Dardúr now needs a Badge of Command and an ashen Gorthorog-horn to complete your reward.\n",
[986]="7006C535\n1\tCollect wight finger-bones from the Dead at Nirgambâr ([see journal]/5)\030Collect wight hand bones from the Dead at Nirgambâr ([see journal]/10)\tMeliri asked you to go to Nirgambâr to retrieve the hand bones and finger-bones of wights. She and Zidemel believe it will quiet the restless spirit of her dead husband and absolve her in preparation for the return of a great king.\n2\tReturn the bones you collected to Meliri in Jirush\tYou collected the hand bones and fingerbones of the wights at Nirgambâr. Return to Meliri listening to Zidemel preach in Jirush and give them to her.\n",
[987]="7002F978\n1\tTalk to Ides\tIdes can be found training at the mill, north of the Rohirrim training grounds, at the northern edge of the Norcrofts. Edwulf has given you control of training Ides, but has counselled you about her headstrong nature.\n2\tDefeat Orcs (total: 5)\tOrcs can be found throughout the Norcrofts. Ides has tasked you with dispatching Orcs in a timely fashion, in order to prove yourself to her. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n3\tReturn to Ides at the training ground\tIdes can be found training at the mill, north of the Rohirrim training grounds, at the northern edge of the Norcrofts. You have surpassed the challenge set forth by Ides, and she awaits your return.\n",
[988]="7006819F\n1\tAdminister the salve to Nekarkul on the shore to the west\tElder Ilaya has asked you to heal a large wounded salamander with the salve given to you by Heshra. The beast can be found west of Khûtra.\n2\tDefeat Nêjagil\tElder Ilaya has asked you to heal a large wounded salamander with the salve given to you by Heshra. The beast can be found west of Khûtra.\n3\tReturn to Elder Ilaya in Khûtra\tReturn to Elder Ilaya in Khûtra.\n",
[989]="7006C581\n1\tCollect Filadal's Mother's necklace\030Avenge Filadal's mother by defeating wrathful spirits ([see journal]/8)\tFiladal told you of being forced to leave the oasis north-west of Shonith as her mother was set to fade. She fled, and only saw her mother surrounded by wrathful spirits before reaching her final rest. She wants a keepsake and vengeance before she fades.\n2\tReturn Filadal's mother's necklace to her at Shonith\tYou recovered the necklace from near one of the trees in the old oasis and defeated a good number of the wrathful spirits there. Return the necklace to Filadal.\n",
[990]="7002EEFB\n1\tTalk to Éorpwald\t\n2\tTalk to Éorpwald\tÉorpwald is hiding behind a wall in Thornhope. You should escort Éorpwald to safety.\n3\tTalk to Éorpwald at Béortnoth's camp\tÉorpwald is at Béortnoth's camp, outside of Thornhope. You should speak with Éorpwald when you return to Béortnoth's camp.\n",
[991]="70047F44\n1\tComplete 'Another Lovely Year' (total: 3)\tEvery day there is something to do during the Anniversary Festival. Come and join everyone and participate in many Anniversary Festival activities for three more days!\n2\tTalk to Waldo Rumble\tWaldo Rumble would like to thank you for your continued participation in the Anniversary Festival.\n",
[992]="70047F4B\n1\tComplete 'Another Lovely Year' (total: 3)\tEvery day there is something to do during the Anniversary Festival. Come and join everyone and participate in many Anniversary Festival activities for three more days!\n2\tTalk to Waldo Rumble\tWaldo Rumble would like to thank you for your continued participation in the Anniversary Festival.\n",
})
